MiSTer text in files that are otherwise MIT
-------------------------------------------
  - rtl/tango_core_arcade_template.v, both CONF_STR variants, and sim/tb_arc.inc (the CONF_STR the bench expects,
    and a comment quoting it): the entries "T[0],Reset;" and "R[0],Reset and close OSD;", as in Template_MiSTer's
    Template.sv (https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Template_MiSTer; its header: GNU General Public License, version 2
    or (at your option) any later version), the entries most MiSTer cores carry.
  - rtl/tango_core_arcade_template.v, comments: quotes of two CONF_STR lines of Arcade-Galaga_MiSTer's
    Arcade-Galaga.sv, "J1,Fire,Start 1P,Start 2P,Coin,Pause;" and "jn,A,Start,Select,R,L;"
    (https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Arcade-Galaga_MiSTer; the file's header: "Port to MiSTer", "Copyright (C) 2017
    Sorgelig", GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later version).
  - fixtures/Arcade Template Test.mra, a comment: a quote of the <buttons> line of MiSTer's Galaxian .mra,
    <buttons default="A,Start,Select,R,B,L" names="Fire,Start 1P,Start 2P,Coin,Test,Pause">, as an example of
    MiSTer's per-game button override.
  - sim/tb_menu.cpp (the CONF_STR the launcher core must return, in the bench's launcher session): the text of the
    framework's Video page entries, "Aspect ratio,Original,Full Screen" and "Scale,Normal,V-Integer,
    Narrower HV-Integer,Wider HV-Integer", which come from sys-tango (tango_video_opts.vh; sys-tango's NOTICE,
    "MiSTer data in files that are otherwise MIT", names their sources in Template_MiSTer's Template.sv and the
    MiSTer cores).  The core's scaler build carries the same entries through sys-tango.


Following other projects' behaviour
-----------------------------------
These files are the Tango authors' code (MIT); they follow documented or observed behaviour of other projects,
which they cite:
  - The menu string format (CONF_STR, with its "DIP" and "J1" entries) and the core interface are MiSTer's
    (sys-tango's NOTICE); the .mra format of fixtures/Arcade Template Test.mra is MiSTer's arcade ROM description.
  - rtl/tango_core_arcade_template.v and sim/tb_pad_row.v: the joystick bit order and the button-name mapping of
    Main_MiSTer (input.h, joymapping.cpp), as the comments cite them; the native 288 x 224 raster (384 x 264 total)
    is Galaga's video timing as Arcade-Galaga_MiSTer's rtl/gen_video.vhd has it.
  - sim/tb_menu.cpp and its *.inc sessions: the BL616 side of the link as the FPGA Companion firmware (Apache-2.0)
    and the Tango firmware (firmware-tango, GPL-3.0-or-later) drive it.


ROMs: none.  The .mra fixture's only ROM part is 16 bytes written inline in the file, the ASCII text
"TANGO-A5-ROM-OK!"; sim/streams/empty.bin is an empty file.
